\ A runtime redefinition of a const prelude binding refuses with `cannot-redefine-const` on every
\ tier. `constraint-info` is a `struct{ }` type word the prelude defines, so its binding carries
\ the const marker. The const guard reads the visible scope first and the baked base scope when
\ that misses, so an interpreter-free binary, which holds the prelude in no frame, refuses with
\ the same error instead of reporting a shadow whose `override` hint a const word cannot honor.
\
\ The redefinition sits inside a word body called from top level, so it fires while the file
\ runs. The `use` gives the entry file an import. The bare call is the file's last statement, so
\ the raise stays in tail position on every tier.

use { taken: } "def_over_import_mod.1z" ;

taken .

redefine-const: ( -- ) [ constraint-info: ( -- n ) [ 0 ] ; ] ;

redefine-const
